<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Concertación</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1988">1988</a>–<a href="/years/2013">2013</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Concertación de Partidos por la Democracia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Concertación was a coalition of Chilean centre-left parties, including the Christian Democrats and the Socialists, formed to oppose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-pinochet">Augusto Pinochet</a> in the plebiscite of 1988. It won every presidential election from 1989 to 2005, governing under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patricio-aylwin">Patricio Aylwin</a>, Eduardo Frei Ruiz-Tagle, Ricardo <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lagos">Lagos</a> and Michelle Bachelet until 2010. It was succeeded by the New Majority coalition in 2013.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/concertacion.jpg" alt="Concertación" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rakela / Vectorized: LordRM · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Concertacion.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
